        "original_id": "82d123f1-cc99-5320-8418-2666909e8277",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Nevada School of Law at Old College, Reno Gazette-Journal, Nevada Appeal, Gannett Company\n- Places: Reno, Nevada, Carson City, Nevada\n- People: Henry Rust Mighels\n- Concepts: Sagebrush School\n\nFacts:\n- After its first year, the Nevada School of Law at Old College moved from the former St. Thomas Aquinas Parochial School to its permanent home in the old Reno Gazette-Journal newspaper plant.\n- The Gannett Company donated the old Reno Gazette-Journal newspaper plant to the Nevada School of Law at Old College.\n- The Reno Gazette-Journal is the main daily newspaper for Reno, Nevada.\n- The Reno Gazette-Journal is owned by the Gannett Company.\n- The Nevada Appeal is Nevada's third-largest newspaper, behind the Las Vegas Review-Journal and the Reno Gazette-Journal.\n- Henry Rust Mighels was a writer of the Sagebrush School and served as editor and publisher of the Nevada Appeal in Carson City, Nevada.",
